  "description": "What: CE-1967 (user report: a bulldozer driving over soldiers only knocked them down; they stood up after it passed) - on bt-range a 49 t bulldozer (TKB 112) is ordered north from (150,100) to (150,150) at 4 m/s; 'Victim' stands on its line at (150,120), 'Bystander' 7 m east of it at (157,120); both hold (no brain reaction, so the run-over is not avoided by the man). Judge: the dozer reaches its point; the Victim is DEAD once the hull has passed over him (a heavy hull crushes what it drives over, R-2138) and never stands up again; the Bystander, beside the 4.3 m blade, is untouched. Fail: the Victim alive after the dozer passed (the defect), or the Bystander hurt. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh ua-dozer-runover"
 },
